course: dictionary
lesson: 1790
title: Context clues: cloak
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word cloak has two jobs. As a noun, it is a loose coat with no sleeves that hangs from the shoulders and is fastened at the neck. As a verb, it means to cover or hide something. You can work out which one you need by looking at the words around it.
explain: «Do the same if you find your neighbour's donkey or cloak or anything else they have lost.» Here, the words neighbour's and lost show that a cloak is something a person owns and can misplace. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A cloak fits, so cloak is a thing, a noun.
explain: «Keep it until they come looking for it, and then give it back.» The clue is give it back. You do not keep a cloak for ever. You return it to the person who lost it. Read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: A cloak is a loose coat without sleeves, fastened at the neck.
fact: As a verb, «cloak» means to cover or hide something, as in «cloaked in mist».
fact: A cloakroom is a place where you leave your coats.
fact: «Under the cloak of» means hidden by something, such as «under the cloak of darkness».
exercise: «Do the same if you find your neighbour's donkey or cloak or anything else they have lost.» In this sentence, what is a cloak? | A kind of donkey | A type of food | *A loose coat that someone owns | A map of the land
exercise: «Keep it until they come looking for it, and then give it back.» What must you do with something you have found? | *Give it back to its owner | Throw it away | Sell it to a shop | Hide it for ever
exercise: Find and copy one word that shows the cloak belongs to someone else. | donkey | find | anything | *neighbour's
test: The mountain was cloaked in cloud. What does cloaked mean here? | Dropped | Lit up | Cleaned | *Covered
test: What is a cloakroom? | A room with a bed | A room for cooking | *A room where you leave coats | A room for swimming
exam: A cloak hangs from the shoulders and is fastened at the neck. Which body part does a cloak hang from? | Knees | *Shoulders | Feet | Head
